A lookup routine narrows its window with this fragment:
while (lo <= hi) {
  int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
  if (data[mid] == target) { return mid; }
  if (data[mid] > target) { _____; }
  else { lo = mid + 1; }
}
Which line belongs in the blank?

An insertion pass slides larger values one slot to the right with this fragment:
int key = data[i];
int j = i - 1;
while (j >= 0 && data[j] > key) {
  _____
}
data[j + 1] = key;
Which statement belongs in the blank?

A frequency map keeps distinct keys and a parallel list of counts:
ArrayList<Character> keys = new ArrayList<>();
ArrayList<Integer> counts = new ArrayList<>();
for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {
  int at = keys.indexOf(c);
  if (at < 0) { keys.add(c); counts.add(1); }
  else { counts.set(at, _____); }
}
Which expression completes the update?

A helper copies one array into another of the same length:
int[] src = {1, 2, 3};
int[] dst = new int[src.length];
for (int i = 0; i < src.length; i++) {
  _____
}
Which statement belongs in the blank?

A minimum scan over an int array seeds its running value:
int smallest = _____;
for (int v : data) {
  if (v < smallest) { smallest = v; }
}
Which seed stays correct for any int data?

A range minimum must consider only the slots from lo through hi:
int[] data = {0, 5, 7, 9, 8};
int lo = 2;
int hi = 4;
int smallest = _____;
for (int i = lo; i <= hi; i++) {
  if (data[i] < smallest) { smallest = data[i]; }
}
Which seed reports the minimum of the range?

A helper counts how many times one letter appears between two bounds of a word:
String word = "abracadabra";
int from = 0;
int to = 3;
int count = 0;
for (int i = from; i ____ to; i++) {
  if (word.charAt(i) == 'a') { count++; }
}
System.out.print(count);
Which condition makes the count cover every slot from from through to?
